{"entity":"epic","version":1,"id":"encrypted-custody","revision":1,"type":"aep.entity.create/v1","from_state":null,"to_state":"draft","changed":{"body":"## Outcome\n\nA public service stores encrypted secret values in PostgreSQL, authenticates people and Kubernetes workloads, and exposes safe metadata, revocation and cryptographic deletion.\n\n## Acceptance\n\nA released service survives restart, refuses cross-tenant or reveal access, and serves its documented API over encrypted PostgreSQL state.\n","summary":"Publish tenant-scoped encrypted custody for user and workload lifecycle.","title":"Encrypted secret custody service"},"args":{"command":"create-entity","data":{"body":"## Outcome\n\nA public service stores encrypted secret values in PostgreSQL, authenticates people and Kubernetes workloads, and exposes safe metadata, revocation and cryptographic deletion.\n\n## Acceptance\n\nA released service survives restart, refuses cross-tenant or reveal access, and serves its documented API over encrypted PostgreSQL state.\n","status":"draft","summary":"Publish tenant-scoped encrypted custody for user and workload lifecycle.","title":"Encrypted secret custody service"},"entity_type":"aep.epic/v1","locator":"ep://planning/store/epic/encrypted-custody"},"payload":{"actor":"human:timo","at":1788260135784,"causation":"cmd-new-epic-encrypted-custody","change":{"change":"created","status":"draft"},"correlation":"protocol-artifact-new","event_id":"epic:encrypted-custody@1#0~7e739ffbf03b7616","executor":null,"recorded_at":"2026-09-01T10:55:35Z"}}
